From 15554144c50c85d21ca101b35df4126e99bfef3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Schuldesz <paulschuldesz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:29:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH milos-linux v1 1/3] media: qcom: camss: csiphy-3ph: Drop C-PHY
 rate settings from the Milos D-PHY table
To: Jorijn van der Graaf <jorijnvdgraaf@catcrafts.net>

lane_regs_milos, the D-PHY (2-phase) lane table for Milos, ends with 36
per-data-rate AFE/CDR/settle entries taken from the downstream
datarate_221_500Msps table. Downstream (Fairphone camera-kernel,
cam_csiphy_core.c) only applies those rate tables in 3-phase mode
(cam_csiphy_cphy_data_rate_config() is gated on csiphy_3phase): they are
C-PHY settings in symbols per second, not D-PHY Mbps settings. Writing
them while the PHY runs in D-PHY mode can break reception.

Remove them from the D-PHY table. The remaining 92 entries match the
downstream D-PHY mode-select, common and 2-phase sequences in order,
value and flags (apart from the SKEW_CAL entries, which the generic code
already skips). The C-PHY table lane_regs_milos_3ph is unchanged.

With this change and the two following CSID/VFE fixes the Fairphone 6
front camera (S5KKD1 on CSIPHY3, D-PHY) streams; the rear IMX896 and
OV13B10 keep working.

Downstream reference: Fairphone camera-kernel 670223e10713,
drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_csiphy/include/cam_csiphy_2_2_1_hwreg.h

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c         | 43 +------------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 42 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
